# Proper Testing

When code changes require tests:

## Do

- Write tests next to the code (`#[cfg(test)] mod tests`) or in `tests/`
- Follow existing crate test structure
- Use `cargo test` conventions
- Name integration files `tests/<behavior>.rs`
- Name unit tests `fn test_*` or descriptive snake_case

## Do Not

- Create adhoc test scripts in project root
- Write temporary `check_*.rs` binaries
- Create `verify_*.rs` throwaway crates
- Add test code to `fn main()` in examples unless the example is the lesson

## Test Location

```
src/
  lib.rs                 # unit tests in #[cfg(test)]
  <module>.rs            # module-level unit tests
tests/
  <behavior>.rs          # integration tests
```

## Example

```rust
// src/ownership.rs
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn borrow_does_not_move() {
        // Test implementation
    }
}
```
